%N A141329 Infinite array read by antidiagonals: a(m,n) = the smallest positive integer that is >= max(m,n) and is non-coprime to both m and n.
%C A141329 The first row of this array is row 2. The first column of this array is column 2.
%C A141329 a(m,n) <= m*n, with equality if and only if m and n are distinct primes. - _Robert Israel_, Jul 31 2026
%H A141329 Robert Israel, <a href="/A141329/b141329.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10012</a> (first 141 antidiagonals, flattened)
%p A141329 f:= proc(m,n) local t;
%p A141329   for t from max(m,n) do
%p A141329     if igcd(t,m) > 1 and igcd(t,n) > 1 then return t fi
%p A141329   od
%p A141329 end proc:
%p A141329 Matrix(10,10,(i,j) -> f(i+1,j+1)); # _Robert Israel_, Jul 31 2026
%Y A141329 Cf. A141327, A141328.
